\label{lem:mixed-product-formula}
Let $E_1,E_2\subseteq F$ have finite colength. Regarding
$E_1E_2$ as a submodule of
$F^2=\operatorname{Sym}_R^2(F)$, one has
\[
\widetilde e_{\mathrm{BR}}(E_1E_2;N)
=
\sum_{i=0}^{q}
\binom{q}{i}
e_{\mathrm{BR}}
\left(E_1^{[q-i]},E_2^{[i]};N\right).
\]

\label{prop:general-minkowski-br}

Let $E_1,E_2\subsetneq F$ have finite colength, and set
\(
I_j=\operatorname{Ann}_R(F/E_j)=(E_j:_RF)
\,\,(j=1,2).
\)
Then, for all integers $r,s\geq1$,
\[
\begin{aligned}
&\sum_{i=0}^{q}\binom qi
e_{\mathrm{BR}}(E_1^{[q-i]},E_2^{[i]};N)
r^{q-i}s^i\leq \binom qd(r+s)^{p-1}
\left(
r\,e(I_1;N)^{1/d}
+s\,e(I_2;N)^{1/d}
\right)^d.
\end{aligned}
\]
